Design: I propose adding simple test-time augmentation (horizontal flip) when extracting embeddings. Specifically, for each image we compute embeddings using the original and horizontally flipped versions (by applying a deterministic flip before the standard preprocessing), and average these embeddings before training the classifier and making predictions. This TTA approach can reduce overfitting and improve robustness. We will update the embedding extraction in both training and the predict() function accordingly, preserving the 5-fold CV evaluation and printing AUROC scores.
